I'd started yet another game, as a doppelganger wizard (I love being
able to self-polymorph at will), and things were going generally well.
Nothing exactly special, but I had a good feeling about the game. I had
an AC of about 1 or so normally, but I spent a lot of time polymorphed,
and I had a pet kmodo dragon, and a pet marilith.

Anyway, all was going fine, until I reached minetown (while level 7),
polymorphed into a marilith, when I got the message 'you feel monsters
are aware of your presence', which kinda confused me, as I though you
could only get that from quaffing a cursed potion of invisibility...

Anyway, I went round a corner, and ran straight into an invisible
titan, and I thought I could take it as I was a marilith and had 2
quite good pets, but it cut me off into a 1 square wide space, so I was
on my own, then weakened me. I tried to put it to sleep, but it wasn't
affected, and it hit me again, so I returned to doppelganger form, so I
tried to run, by I didn't displace my marilith, and it made me weak, so
I dropped my dwarfen mithril as I was burdened, and it killed me. At
that point I found that the amulet I was wearing was life saving, so I
thought I was really lucky, and ran for it, hoping my marilith and
komodo dragon would hold it off so I could get to the upstairs, and I
was running when I got hit by a blast of fire, which nearly killed me,
so I prayed, got healed, then a few turns later, I found myself getting
mauled to death, which turned out to be an invisible hellhound.

As far as I can tell, I didn't really do anything wrong (except try to
attack the titan, but I didn't know how strong they were), and I was
just unlucky - I mean, come on, an invisible titan, and an invisible
hellhound, in Minetown?!

Sorry about the probably excessive detail, but I was really annoyed at
this one.



